<table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Nov 3, 2003 :: Grats Ckaii on your flamey sword!!</div><P>Reide took the pictures, since I have old world models on and they do not show your true sexiness. But grats on finally getting your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics10/fieryavenger.jpg">Fiery Avenger</A>!! </P>
<P>Thanks all for keeping up the pace of dragon kills so we can get everyone set who wants to go! Grats Jakr on your talisman... put on your buffing pants! :)</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Nov 5, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Nov 2, 2003 :: Only Reide could trigger two wars at once...</div><P>We gathered up for another Ring War, this one for Reide. Somehow there was a small burp or something in the script, and two wars triggered simulteanously... two seneschals, two sets of heroes, and double the spawns. Well, that's somewhat interesting. Let's make it more interesting.. we only had 22 people there when we started. </P>
<P>As people logged on, they came running down down to help. Thanks to our&nbsp;friends Iionz, Sulien, Barreck&nbsp;and Daemonspawn&nbsp;for coming along. We invited a group of folks doing faction work into the raid so they could have a heads up which direction the spawns were coming from, since it was crazy! Thanks Aniha, Tatekei, Loginue and Krizel... hope I didn't miss anyone! :)</P>
<P>When all was said and done, we were victorious and not a single hero (either one!) died! It was a rough war, but a lot of fun! Everyone truly showed just how stubborn we are. Grats Reide on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/ring_dain_frostweaver.jpg">Ring of Dain Frostreaver IV</A>, Jakr on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/rpics/crown_of_narandi.jpg">Crown of Narandi</A>, Bearspirit on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/Choker_of_the_Wretched.jpg">Choker of the Wretched</A>, Garetjax on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/narandis_lance.jpg">Narandi's Lance</A>, Antroe on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/faceguard_bentos_hero.jpg">Faceguard of Bentos the Hero</A>&nbsp;and Beryllin and Garacaius on the GREED rolls for the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=6789">Eye of Narandi</A> and <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/earringfrozenskull.jpg">Earring of the Frozen Skull</A>! Sadly for us, only one set of heroes gave the reward, the second sat there. Will add some pictures later&nbsp;that I know Myschief took!</P>
<P><IMG alt="Double the Fun!" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/war2.gif" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>Leveling grats to Bashiuss on 60 and Grave Lord!<BR>Lentor on 64!<BR>Garrich on 54!<BR>Tristastar on 48! <BR>Wonderous can fill in what I've missed! /smirks</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Nov 6, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Nov 1, 2003 :: Lend the Giver and Sontalak dead!</div><P>Yelinak decided not to show up, so we decided to head on over to do Lend the Keeper again. Sont was up already, so we did a quick kill of him first. Grats Reide on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/sontalaks_talisman.JPG">Sontalak's talisman</A>! After that we headed inside and had a nearly flawless kill against Lend. Everyone worked together and did a great job! </P>
<P>Grats Aridius on your new <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/breastplate_superiority.jpg">Breastplate of Superiority</A>, Beryllin on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/ringofrelkententinar.jpg">Ring of Relkententinar</A> and SG on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/lendiniarastalisman.jpg">Lendiniara's Talisman</A>!</P>
<P><IMG alt="" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/lend0.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>After that, SG led some folks to Kael to work on their factions. A bit later, Kithik led folks on Burrower Watch 03! Sadly, there were no sightings of the elusive bug. Folks hung in there and amused themselves for some time though! Then Cassana decided she needed a little head, and everyone wanted to watch! Onto Plane of Disease where Barreck's arch enemy, Rallius Rattican was smooshed. And, irony of all ironies.. grats Sonaddor on the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/arachnid_antennae.gif">Arachnid Antennae</A>... the one item we used to kill him for over and over for Barreck. And grats Cass on his head and completing your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/intermediatestealthmanual.jpg">Intermediate Stealth Manual</A>!!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Nov 5, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Oct 31, 2003 :: Klandicar, dreading our arrival again</div>Thanks for folks who gathered up and killed Klandicar again! Grats Balut on your talisman! <p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Nov 5, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Oct 30, 2003 :: Killing Erudites for Prizes!</div><P>Well, ok, despite that Arglar would prob have wanted that.. it really wasn't killing Erudites for fun and prizes. Thanks Saragoth for gathering a whole bunch of nice items and cash and donating them in a raffle for the guild! Lots of folks walked off with nice stuff and we *almost* kept Fezz from winning. He managed to win something though :(</P>
<P>After that, Raihn found Sontalak keeping watch over ToV. So we gathered up and killed them yet again! Grats Lushissx on a nice new talisman!!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Nov 5, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Oct 28, 2003 :: Three More Keys done!</div><P>Nice work all for coming out and getting three more dragons for three more keys! Sorry Ahyth that it put the General on hold... again. :(</P>
<P>Our daily check of Zlandicar found him up and alone in his lair. So we tried to move folks quickly to Dragon Necropolis to get him for ourselves. We were in luck, despite not moving as fast as we could. Thanks Zelcon for being my master looter tonight. Zland gave up <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/zlandicars_talisman.jpg">his Talisman</A> for Mahrsan tonight. He also had some of his better drops! Grats Tryder on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/firstbroodtalisman.jpg">First Brood Talisman</A>, Feskan on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=4640">Frakadar's Talisman</A> (to make <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/shroud_dar_brood.jpg">Shroud of Dar Brood</A>), Cassana on a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/cowl_of_mortality.jpg">Cowl of Mortality</A> and Lokki on a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/zlandicars_heart.JPG">Zlandicar's Heart</A>!</P>
<P><IMG alt="Zland! Not Feet!" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/zland03.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>We zoned out and killed Klandicar, and even got to kill off Wonderous there! /smirks Grats Wonderous on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/Klandicar_s_Talisman.jpg">Klandicar's Talisman</A>! </P>
<P><IMG alt="Kland! Not Feet!" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/kland03.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>Headed over to Sontalak, who we've so far just killed with ease. Well, tonight he gave us some trouble. Had a little confusion about heading up to him while KOS and he aggroed the raid early (song aggro, I do believe, transferred from the KOS person). Vaea, who wasn't even in position yet, was able to just rezz folks back and rebuff to go again. Second time around he decided to take it out on Vaea, she went down early, and Valoura can't resist any of those effects from Sont, so Sont ate at our raid slowly so by 2pct only two people were left standing... Lairiel and Wonderous. Wond got adds off of him and Lair chased it around. Wond died but was bound by our bodies and started clicking us in. We threw on armor, some ran naked and unhealed, and we ran to Lairiel's aid and killed the bitch. Stupid dragons, don't they know how stubborn we are? Fittingly enough, grats Lairiel on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/sontalaks_talisman.JPG">Sontalak's Talisman</A>! </P>
<P><IMG alt="Sont! Not feet!" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/sont03.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Nov 5, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Oct 27, 2003 :: Some Level Updates, missing some I'm sure!</div><P>Grats Talyss on 65 and Storm Warden!<BR>Grats Jenrenee on 64!<BR>Grats Dorina and Cimmy on 62!<BR>Grats Juhel on 59!<BR>Grats Valoura on 54!<BR>Grats Edenstar and Ahyth on 53!<BR>Grats Moordread on 51 and Heretic!</P>
<P>I know I've missed a bunch, apologies!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Oct 26, 2003 :: Clearing of Veeshan's Peak</div><P>We finally found some time to get back to VP and do some serious clearing. Okies, so I got folks up at the crack of dawn to go there, with much complaining (mostly from Zavitar!)... details. /smirks</P>
<P>Fourteen of us (and 4 bots.. 3 clerics and 1 druid for ports out for those without potions or gate ability) dragged our butts out of bed early for this. We had Lokki and Mahrsan for pulling, Reide for our tank, Colwn for our split tank, Vorne and Jen for even more tanking if we needed it. Raihndance scouted and opened doors for us, Kithik lent his voice, Beryllin made swiss cheese out of many dragons and their brood, Xman and his pet blew shit up... well, I bet the pet did most of the work! Drakshar was there to slow and buff and dot and click that cudgel (then the new toy) nonstop, Zavitar mezzed anything mezzable and carried the enchanter team, and we even brought a live cleric too.. Wonderous! I just sat in back and took pictures and turned Reide into a guktan. /nods</P>
<P>Decided to go for that pain in the ass greenie first... Hoshkar! Reide came up with a clever plan, and it&nbsp;worked perfect. Our pullers delivered a lovely dragon package and we wrapped it up! Folks saved the following from rotting: Kantar and his <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/Fatesealer.JPG">Fatesealer</A>, Vorne and his <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/Sword_of_the_Shissar.jpg">Sword of the Shissar</A>, Beryllin and <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=3565">Veldrak's Shortblade</A>. </P>
<P><IMG alt=Hoshkar! hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/vphosh.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>From there, we headed up to our friend Silverwing, the mad gater! He gated I think 4 times, but no worries, we just followed Reide the Insane into the hall outside his lair and let him keep pulling him out to fight. His annoying gating habits at least gave Drakshar&nbsp;a nice new toy.. <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics14/hammer_dragonborn.jpg">Hammer of the Dragonborn</A>! Meeka nabbed a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics14/robe_smothering.JPG">Robe of Smothering</A>, Reide saved&nbsp;<A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics14/scimitar_lifestealing.jpg">The Scimitar of Lifestealing</A> from rot, but don't think anyone was even willing to save the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=2713">Dragon Claw Main Gauche</A> this time. </P>
<P><IMG alt=Silverwing! hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/vpsilver.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>From there, we headed down to find Phara Dar. Which we sort of did. Some may say that while we were fighting, he kind of found us. They would be correct. No matter, Reide grabbed Phara Dar and we prepared to fight the hardest dragon in VP with an add (or maybe two, I forget). Wow, he was disappointing. I gave up and just decided to take pictures instead! At least he gave up a worthwhile drop! Grats Vaea on your <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=3555">Shroud of Veeshan</A>! I think Beryllin and Kithik broke down and each saved a&nbsp;<A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/dfpics/Claw_of_Phara_Dar.gif">Claw of Phara Dar</A> from rotting. </P>
<P><IMG alt="Phara Dar!" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/vpphara.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>Headed down to Nexona next. Or maybe Nexona headed up to us... with several adds. Yah, not sure why, but Nexona decided to grab some flappy dragon, two racnars (one unmezzable type) and a guardian wurm with him. We kiled him, the flappy thing (pretty sure a flappy thing was there too), Vorne, Mahrsan&nbsp; and Meeka were the last standing, if I didn't miss anyone. Vorne and Mahrsan managed to get the guardian wurm to 3pct, we got Wonderous camped out, and I did my best to keep one racnar mezzed, and the other aggroed on me while trying to arcane rune tank it, but eventually it killed me, then went back for my boys. No matter though! Wonderous logged back in, rezzed us up, Kithik mezzed a flappy thing while we medded and buffed and we dealt crap loot! Dracolokki looted the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/rpics/bo_staff_of_trorsmang.jpg">Bo Staff of Trorsmang</A>, Vaea saved the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/sprinkler_suffering.jpg">Sprinkler of Suffering</A> from rot, and Lokki and Reide both looted a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/db/item.html?item=6064">Robe of Adversity</A> to torment necros. </P>
<P><IMG alt=Nexona! hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/vpnexo.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>Wonderous, in camping out and saving the raid, must have decided it was time to run around and pacify every mob on the way. As we finally ask where the impatient cleric has gone and what the hell is going on... we hear that Druushk has been aggroed... and for a shock, the pacified roaming mob he ran past aggroed on the fight, as well as the other pacified mob at the bottom. Bad bad cleric! We ran down the ramp looking for our wayward troublemaker. However, since we were not even remotely prepared for this fight, karma played a cruel joke. Vorne got charmed and killed Wonderous. Think Wonderbutt was the only casualty, could be wrong! Reide got himself a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/bloodorchidkatana.JPG">Blood Orchid Katana</A> and spent the rest of his time once outside casting Spirit of the Wolf on anyone and everyone. You'd think he won Time loot. Meeka and Zavitar each saved a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/shissar_focus_staff.JPG">Shissar Focus Staff</A> from rotting. </P>
<P><IMG alt=Druushk! hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/vpdruu.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>On to the last dragon left, Xygoz. At least we actually intentionally pulled him. Admire the lovely shade of baby crap, as Raihndance put it. Raihndance saved a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/razor_sharp_short_sword.jpg">Razor Sharp Short Sword</A> from rot, and Mahrsan did the same for a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/Smoldering_Cudgel.JPG">Smouldering Cudgel</A>. Not sure if anyone actually bothered to rescue the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/spear_constriction.jpg">Spear of Constriction</A>. </P>
<P><IMG alt=Xygoz! hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/vpxyg.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>We also got many spells, and a few other trinkets from mini named mobs. Grats Kantar on a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/drake_claw_necklace.jpg">Drake Claw Necklace</A>, Jenrenee on a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/runed_earring_of_the_sky.jpg">Runed Earring of the Sky</A>, Mahrsan on the greed roll for Lava Totem of Veeshan, Xman on the greed roll for <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/sandals_of_ire.jpg">Sandals of Ire</A>, Ceyria on the greed roll for <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/fpics/lavastone_ring.jpg">Lavastone Ring</A> (VP version). We strolled out over the teleporter pad and some of us probably headed back to bed. Nice work all, and a fun morning. </P>
<P>Later on we headed over and killed our favorite dragon! Grats Divan on the talisman, and the folks that won the greed rolls on the loot!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Oct 27, 2003</p></td></tr></table><p /><span class="page-scroll">Pages: <a href='news.asp?page=10'>&laquo;</a>&nbsp;<a href='news.asp?page=1'>1</a>...<a href='news.asp?page=9'>9</a> <a href='news.asp?page=10'>10</a> 11 <a href='news.asp?page=12'>12</a> <a href='news.asp?page=13'>13</a>...<a href='news.asp?page=15'>15</a>&nbsp;<a href='news.asp?page=12'>&raquo;</a></span></td>
